{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggH2AkGAyCpH9aaRmxNg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `split_cents` in `money.py`. It now hands the remainder out one grosz at a time to the first people in the list, so the shares always add up to the total.\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\nI ran a quick check on four cases, and the shares sum to the total in each:\n- `split_cents(100, 3)` returns `[34, 33, 33]`.\n- `split_cents(100, 4)` returns `[25, 25, 25, 25]`.\n- `split_cents(1, 3)` returns `[1, 0, 0]`.\n- `split_cents(0, 2)` returns `[0, 0]`.\n\nThe first person in the list always gets the extra grosz. If you want that spread differently, for example by rotating who gets it, that's a separate change.\n\nI haven't committed anything. The tests are still to do next sprint, as you said. A regression test for the `(100, 3)` case would be a good first one."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":591,"cache_read_input_tokens":17923,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":591},"output_tokens":327,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"434dba7a-6ab9-44ad-96c4-8455fe7b15fb","uuid":"0bf6cdf5-ed2d-4ffc-80c9-4f52576ad158","timestamp":"2026-11-03T16:03:13.564Z","request_id":"req_011CggH2AWdda1TJG7p7jE2i"}
